 "text": "Latiaran is an Irish goddess or heroine. A standing stone in the shape of a heart stands near a small holy well. The well is named for Saint Latiaran. A legend says she was modest. She carried hot coals in her apron. A smith praised the shape of her ankles. She dropped the apron and the stone fell upright. Then she vanished under it. The stone is called the heart of Latiaran. It stands near the graveyard at Cullen. Hot coals and her sisters mark her as a fire goddess. Her sisters were Lasair and Inghean Bhuidhe.",
